    "fiber": {
      "word": "FIBER; FIBRE",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "One of the delicate, threadlike portions of which the tissues of plants and animals are in part constituted; as, the fiber of flax or of muscle.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "Any fine, slender thread, or threadlike substance; as, a fiber of spun glass; especially, one of the slender rootlets of a plant.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "Sinew; strength; toughness; as, a man of real fiber. Yet had no fibers in him, nor no force. Chapman.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A general name for the raw material, such as cotton, flax, hemp, etc., used in textile manufactures. Fiber gun, a kind of steam gun for converting, wood, straw, etc., into fiber. The material is shut up in the gun with steam, air, or gas at a very high pressure which is afterward relieved suddenly by letting a lid at the muzzle fly open, when the rapid expansion separates the fibers. the arts, as hemp, flax, ramie, agave, etc.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        }
      ],
